From a38d4054233d7092c0f39b3ba1435eefd11ca86d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GGEZUS <coelho.b.ricardo@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 23:17:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 14/15] feat(input): single-finger edge and corner swipe
 gestures
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replace the bottom-edge-only swipe with eight zones: a finger starting
within 48px of any output edge swiping inward past 40px fires that
zone's action, and a finger starting in a corner square swiping
diagonally inward past 20px on both axes fires the corner's action.
Mostly-straight swipes near a corner deliberately fire nothing, so the
adjacent edges stay usable up to the corner.

- `touchscreen-edge-swipe { bottom/top/left/right { ...; } }` and the
  new `touchscreen-corner-swipe { top-left/top-right/bottom-left/
  bottom-right { ...; } }` each bind any niri action per zone; zones
  left unbound are inert and touches there deliver normally. This
  replaces the old `touchscreen-edge-swipe { spawn ... }` argv node —
  a breaking config change (the spawn form never really worked).
- Corners win over edges when the start is within 48px of two adjacent
  edges; zones are classified per output from the touch position, so
  multi-output and output transforms are handled for free.
- The dispatch sequence (action, synthetic lift, swallow grab) and the
  single-finger discipline are unchanged from the bottom-edge swipe.
